# The build dependencies do not include cargo and rustc. The build
# environment installs a pinned Rust toolchain into /usr/opt. The default
# features of ostrya-mountd compile liblzma from its vendored source, and the
# binary links it statically. So the build needs a C compiler from
# build-essential and no -dev package.
Source: ostrya-mountd
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/growler/ostrya

Package: ostrya-mountd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: systemd
Description: composefs mount daemon of ostrya
 ostrya-mountd mounts a commit of an ostrya repository as a composefs tree
 for a caller in its own user namespace, for example a rootless container
 tool. The members of the group ostrya-mount can connect to the daemon.
 .
 This package contains the daemon, its systemd units, and the sysusers.d
 file of the group. The package does not enable the socket unit.
